{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:58:08.390569Z","id":"d3f1310c1b7ffe7ef800e9671d0e26dbaff9382dd3c8ef4483c0e51b55e54531","body":{"detail":"sizes here are the gallery and artifact entries, the eager bridge, the bridge's parts, the question module and the extension. The shell's host chunk (dist/_clax/shell/host-*.js, imported by web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts on ?app=1; 3677 gzip bytes at 647958f22844) loads before the host's first `ready`, which stops the app's say-usable timer, yet it can grow without any budget in web/perf/bundle-budget.json failing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":98},"end":{"line":98},"content_hash":"2de1cdb0a07568b315cc7144cf3b6d9d31094e0681341ea26845036d4f5cfce4"},"suggested_fix":"Measure the chunk artifact-main.ts imports for app mode (its manifest dynamic import) as `host`, and add a `host` entry to web/perf/bundle-budget.json at its size rounded up to 64 bytes.","summary":"App mode's lazy host chunk, on the say-usable path, has no bundle budget","tags":["review","budget","perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:18:50.264732Z","id":"364e662bae6b9b2d9fba0a8b0cba79d1c3d4ce94c2f26a748b0507acc19e37eb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"647958f22844 measures the chunk artifact.html imports for ?app=1, with what it loads beyond the entry, as host, budget 3712 in web/perf/bundle-budget.json. node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after scripts/build-web.sh: 'app host 3639', exit 0; npx vitest run scripts/bundle-size.test.ts: 29 passed, including the new host case (over budget and missing budget both exit 1).","supersedes":"d3f1310c1b7ffe7ef800e9671d0e26dbaff9382dd3c8ef4483c0e51b55e54531","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:06:45.501947Z","id":"7cab4d62ef08f8f9350e87daf9650924c05540072b3265502e9e1f4b8fb076f7","body":{"detail":"plugins/pi/package.json, the repository's other npm package (@empathic/clax-pi), sets publishConfig {access: public}, author, homepage, bugs and keywords. packageJson() sets none of them. A scoped package publishes as restricted unless told otherwise (https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/commands/npm-publish#access); .github/workflows/publish-pi.yml passes --access public itself, but a hand `npm publish` of web/dist-sdk would fail or need the flag. There is also no README in the package, so npm shows no page text.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":71},"content_hash":"b58f20e8bf81cae8829cf34d0c62915a31f57754fe5f761f82f03d0bcb2cbb2e"},"suggested_fix":"Add publishConfig {access: \"public\"}, author, homepage (the repository's web/sdk or docs/usage.md section), bugs and keywords as plugins/pi/package.json has them, and write a README into dist-sdk from a source file under web/sdk.","summary":"The generated package.json lacks fields plugins/pi/package.json carries: publishConfig.access, homepage, bugs, author, keywords","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","npm","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:06:45.501977Z","id":"8e362a06606bcf7b16e58c1dc086ad384414ce4bfbfeff80e9bdd61a869cd4d6","body":{"detail":"@empathic/clax-pi is published by .github/workflows/publish-pi.yml (npm publish --provenance, trusted publishing) as step 20 of scripts/release.sh, with its first version published from the releaser's machine (scripts/release.sh:1071-1086). The SDK package is built (web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs) and versioned from Cargo.toml's [workspace.package] version, but no workflow or release step publishes it, so its first publication has no defined path and would be by hand, without provenance.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"33749ba42505348444064b4d32eaa7575879be8e14d3a27dafcda20e82a3957e"},"suggested_fix":"Add a publish workflow for web/dist-sdk on the model of publish-pi.yml (build //web:dist_sdk at the pin commit, npm publish --provenance --access public) and a release.sh step after the Pi package's.","summary":"Nothing publishes @empathic/clax-sdk: no workflow like publish-pi.yml and no release.sh step","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","npm","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:06:45.502006Z","id":"76643ef265d3ad95c82514be1212a482d9a5383f173e836feba0c620a62d80a1","body":{"detail":"The sources import their siblings without extensions (e.g. web/sdk/src/index.ts imports \"./client\"), so emitTypes adds `.js` (or `/index.js`) to every relative specifier with a regex over the .d.ts text (build-sdk.mjs:140-146) and walks the result. A declaration form the regex does not match (a multi-line `import(` type, an `export =`/`import x = require(...)`) would be left unrewritten; //web:sdk_package (web/sdk/package.test.ts:106-119) would catch a missing `.js` but not a missed file. Its options (build-sdk.mjs:123-127) restate web/tsconfig.json's rather than reading it, so the two can drift.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":122},"end":{"line":155},"content_hash":"70dd140caa83838d88370a6dfa366161f8267793aabd60d27fdc05ae8b10b8f6"},"suggested_fix":"Write `.js` extensions in the relative imports under web/sdk/src, web/overlay/src and the bridge files the overlay reaches, so tsc emits loadable declarations as they are; or read web/tsconfig.json with ts.parseJsonConfigFileContent and override only declaration, emitDeclarationOnly and outDir.","summary":"emitTypes rewrites import specifiers in emitted declarations with a regex, under compiler options separate from web/tsconfig.json","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:11:00.340243Z","id":"68021461b0d538d8857d74724191f8255c555f9833c56b67022ac2e27444b597","body":{"detail":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs:55-71 sets name, version, description, license, repository, type, sideEffects, exports only; writeMetadata (157-163) writes package.json, LICENSE, LICENSES/, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt, no README. plugins/pi/package.json has keywords, author, homepage, bugs and publishConfig {access: public}; .github/workflows/publish-pi.yml:131 runs `npm publish --provenance --access public`. On the default: https://docs.npmjs.com/creating-and-publishing-scoped-public-packages says 'By default, scoped packages are published with private visibility. To publish a scoped package with public visibility, use npm publish --access public.' The URL the finding cites (https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/commands/npm-publish#access) instead gives the default as \"'public' for new packages\" (npm CLI v10 config definition, default null), so cite the scoped-packages page. Kind (suggestion) fits.","kind":"comment","references":"7cab4d62ef08f8f9350e87daf9650924c05540072b3265502e9e1f4b8fb076f7","summary":"confirmed: packageJson() lacks publishConfig.access, author, homepage, bugs, keywords and the package has no README; the cited npm URL says otherwise about the default","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:11:00.340543Z","id":"6c6a65465db699f4fd406bb34e05cf0fc57703372022ff77613474a538e6aec1","body":{"detail":"`grep -rn 'clax-sdk\\|dist-sdk\\|dist_sdk' .github scripts/release.sh` finds nothing; .github/workflows holds ci, deploy-prod, fleet-image, native-check, publish-pi and release only. scripts/release.sh:63 lists step 20 as `gh workflow run publish-pi.yml`, and pi_first_publish (scripts/release.sh:1068-1090, function at 1073) publishes the Pi package's first version locally. docs/usage.md:622-650 ('The SDK package') describes building and linking it but no publishing. web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs:56 reads the version from Cargo.toml [workspace.package]. Line citations correct.","kind":"comment","references":"8e362a06606bcf7b16e58c1dc086ad384414ce4bfbfeff80e9bdd61a869cd4d6","summary":"confirmed: no workflow or release step publishes @empathic/clax-sdk","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:11:00.340858Z","id":"b85712298d5ad4cc14eec9ef94ef69bb4d8e75b84076fa4e46cb787d90c7e974","body":{"detail":"build-sdk.mjs:140-146 rewrites `from`, `import(` and `import \"…\"` specifiers by regex; 123-127 restate options rather than reading web/tsconfig.json (which differs: types vite/client,node,chrome; paths clax-bridge-parts; allowImportingTsExtensions). web/sdk/src/index.ts:6-8 import \"./client\", \"./reporter\", \"./types\" without extensions. Corrections: (1) a multi-line `import(` type is matched, because `\\bimport\\s*\\(\\s*` uses \\s, which spans newlines; `export =` carries no specifier. Only `import x = require(\"…\")` is a real unmatched form, and the ESM sources do not use it. (2) A missed file would not pass //web:sdk_package: web/sdk/package.test.ts:121-146 type-checks an app importing every entry under nodenext and bundler with skipLibCheck unset (line 142), so TypeScript checks the installed package's .d.ts and reports an unresolved or extensionless relative import. Kind (suggestion) fits.","kind":"comment","references":"76643ef265d3ad95c82514be1212a482d9a5383f173e836feba0c620a62d80a1","summary":"confirmed: specifiers are rewritten by regex and the compiler options are restated, but two of the detail's supporting points do not hold","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:11:46.562659Z","id":"386f7ea9e2db6c633e47890bf29b09ae2402ca92d23cb82e16b1df9f0074f135","body":{"detail":"plugins/pi/package.json, the repository's other npm package (@empathic/clax-pi), sets publishConfig {access: public}, author, homepage, bugs and keywords. packageJson() sets none of them. Scoped packages publish with private visibility unless published with --access public (https://docs.npmjs.com/creating-and-publishing-scoped-public-packages); .github/workflows/publish-pi.yml:131 passes --access public itself, but a hand `npm publish` of web/dist-sdk would need the flag. writeMetadata (build-sdk.mjs:157-163) writes no README, so npm shows no page text.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":71},"content_hash":"b58f20e8bf81cae8829cf34d0c62915a31f57754fe5f761f82f03d0bcb2cbb2e"},"suggested_fix":"Add publishConfig {access: \"public\"}, author, homepage (the repository's web/sdk or docs/usage.md section), bugs and keywords as plugins/pi/package.json has them, and write a README into dist-sdk from a source file under web/sdk.","summary":"The generated package.json lacks fields plugins/pi/package.json carries: publishConfig.access, homepage, bugs, author, keywords","supersedes":"7cab4d62ef08f8f9350e87daf9650924c05540072b3265502e9e1f4b8fb076f7","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","npm","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:11:46.656717Z","id":"ec0ee217137b88b146c4da564a87c6f6105f720cc461066ba9f936c3dbac07d3","body":{"detail":"The sources import their siblings without extensions (web/sdk/src/index.ts:6-8 imports \"./client\", \"./reporter\", \"./types\"), so emitTypes adds `.js` (or `/index.js`) to every relative specifier with a regex over the .d.ts text (build-sdk.mjs:140-146) and walks the result. The regex covers `from`, `import(` (across lines) and side-effect imports; `import x = require(\"…\")` is the one form it does not match, which the ESM sources do not use today. A miss would be caught: web/sdk/package.test.ts:121-146 type-checks an app importing every entry without skipLibCheck. The remaining cost is maintenance: the options at build-sdk.mjs:123-127 restate rather than read web/tsconfig.json (which differs in types, paths and allowImportingTsExtensions), and the rewrite is code the package would not need if the sources' relative imports carried `.js`.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":122},"end":{"line":155},"content_hash":"70dd140caa83838d88370a6dfa366161f8267793aabd60d27fdc05ae8b10b8f6"},"suggested_fix":"Write `.js` extensions in the relative imports under web/sdk/src, web/overlay/src and the bridge files the overlay reaches, so tsc emits loadable declarations as they are; or read web/tsconfig.json with ts.parseJsonConfigFileContent and override only declaration, emitDeclarationOnly, outDir and types.","summary":"emitTypes rewrites import specifiers in emitted declarations with a regex, under compiler options separate from web/tsconfig.json","supersedes":"76643ef265d3ad95c82514be1212a482d9a5383f173e836feba0c620a62d80a1","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:13:13.744895Z","id":"57f23d371629b772a3d1a5157a0a917716380660d4ffe77a76700019748b7109","body":{"detail":"Rollup's watcher follows only the modules in the bundle's graph. esbuild erases `import type` and `export type *` before Rollup sees them, so web/sdk/src/types.ts (only types; imported by `import type` from reporter.ts, client.ts, service.ts, model.ts, the Svelte components, and by `export type * from \"./types\"` in sdk/src/index.ts) and web/overlay/src/options.ts (imported by `import type` from overlay/src/main.ts) are not in the graph. Editing either while `node scripts/build-sdk.mjs --watch` runs (which scripts/watch.sh:81 starts for `just watch`) triggers no rebuild, so emitTypes() never runs and web/dist-sdk/types/sdk/src/types.d.ts and types/overlay/src/options.d.ts keep the old declarations; an app that links web/dist-sdk type-checks against them. docs/usage.md:636-637 says the watch build 'rebuilds it on every change to its sources'. Relatedly, cleanOut(out) runs only once (build-sdk.mjs:178) and the build sets emptyOutDir: false, so in watch mode a chunk or declaration file that a later rebuild no longer produces (a renamed chunk under chunks/, a declaration no entry reaches any more) stays in web/dist-sdk.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":165},"end":{"line":175},"content_hash":"e391abf13c3d9baef3af74c1a0e4947cd5dd2a4880bf925282f7e4a26c9391c4"},"suggested_fix":"Give the packageFiles plugin a buildStart hook that calls this.addWatchFile for every non-node_modules source file of the TypeScript program emitTypes() builds (or for every .ts file under web/sdk/src, web/overlay/src and web/bridge/src), and in writeBundle remove files under chunks/ and types/ that the current bundle and declaration set did not write.","summary":"build-sdk.mjs --watch never rebuilds on a change to a type-only module, so types/ goes stale","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:13:13.744955Z","id":"a057dd22b8f18ad4f810f1b2fa5a12b7b67b54830e9ff61ea41fc5aa9bc314ea","body":{"detail":"thirdPartyNotices() (build-sdk.mjs:95-115) fails the build on a bundled Clax module outside web/bridge, web/overlay and web/sdk, the directories LICENSE:65-71 puts under LGPL-2.1-only, and the header comment (build-sdk.mjs:19-21) states that guarantee for the package. emitTypes() applies no such check: its program's rootDir is web/, and visit() accepts any relative specifier whose declaration was emitted, so if an exported type of sdk/src or overlay/src came to reference a type from web/shell or web/contract (AGPL-3.0-only per LICENSE:60-63) or web/extension (GPL-2.0-only), the package would ship types/shell/... or types/extension/... declarations, doc comments included, under the package's LGPL-2.1-only license with no error. web/overlay/src/options.ts exists on this branch precisely so main.d.ts does not reach bridge types; nothing enforces the wider boundary. web/sdk/package.test.ts:106-119 checks only that declarations stay inside the package, not which source directories they come from.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":133},"end":{"line":148},"content_hash":"36835ca0ce82c2e50d5ab6398f3dbda7e58381607514f4cf1647ef8cedf08b09"},"suggested_fix":"In emitTypes' visit(), throw unless `file` starts with one of LICENSED_DIRS followed by `/` (the same list thirdPartyNotices uses), and add an assertion to web/sdk/package.test.ts that every file under types/ lies under types/bridge/, types/overlay/ or types/sdk/.","summary":"The license guard covers bundled JavaScript only: emitTypes() ships declarations of any web/ source the entries' types reach","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:13:13.744983Z","id":"9492ec6db6f9a986f5460ec2aea4ef0cc9bb76b395288001a183e2dfad7cc403","body":{"detail":"Two ways the classification differs from what its comment says. (1) Virtual modules are skipped only when the ID has no `/node_modules/` in it (line 100-102). Vite's CommonJS support wraps a node_modules file in virtual modules whose IDs are `\\0` + the absolute path + a suffix (Vite 6 builds with @rollup/plugin-commonjs, whose wrapId in packages/commonjs/src/helpers.js at https://github.com/rollup/plugins is `(id, suffix) => \\0 + id + suffix`, with suffixes ?commonjs-exports, ?commonjs-module, ?commonjs-proxy and ?commonjs-es-import). Such an ID contains `/node_modules/`, so line 106 adds a root that starts with `\\0`, and line 109's readFileSync(join(root, \"package.json\")) throws Node's invalid-argument error for a path with a null byte. The first CommonJS dependency the overlay bundles (today svelte, esm-env and modern-screenshot are all ESM) would therefore fail the build with an error unrelated to licensing. (2) Vite normalizes module IDs to forward slashes on every platform, but lines 96 and 102 build `nm` and the licensed prefixes with path.sep; on Windows sep is `\\`, so no ID matches either test and the build throws 'the package bundles ..., outside web/bridge, web/overlay, web/sdk' for web/sdk/src/index.ts itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":107},"content_hash":"f747e02e094f686e4d35188a5fa6346627a50cc5d59aef1000fcad5ab28aef8f"},"suggested_fix":"Normalize each ID first: `const file = id.replace(/^\\0/, \"\").split(\"?\")[0]`; compute the package root from `file` with \"/node_modules/\"; compare against `join(web, d).split(sep).join(\"/\") + \"/\"`; and skip only virtual IDs that are not absolute paths (Rollup helpers such as `\\0commonjsHelpers.js`).","summary":"thirdPartyNotices() reads module IDs as raw native paths: a `\\0`-prefixed node_modules ID crashes it, and on Windows every ID fails the license guard","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:13:13.745013Z","id":"8a8d295a030821782b88de92ce8159a660cf7119aae639dce28cadbfafb0f331","body":{"detail":"thirdPartyNotices() decides whether the package may be published at all (it fails on a Clax module outside the LGPL directories) and which licenses it carries (package-root extraction for scoped and nested node_modules paths, the license-file regex, the pnpm and rules_js store layouts). Its only coverage is web/sdk/package.test.ts:71-76, which checks that the notices of one real build name svelte and modern-screenshot; nothing exercises the failure path, a scoped package, a nested node_modules, a query-suffixed ID or a virtual ID. The module runs cleanOut() and vite build() at top level (build-sdk.mjs:177-191), so exporting PACKAGE_NAME and ENTRIES (lines 36, 43) suggests it is meant to be imported, but importing it from a test would wipe and rebuild web/dist-sdk. The repository's scripts keep testable logic importable elsewhere (web/scripts/bundle-size.test.ts drives bundle-size.mjs against fixtures).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":93},"end":{"line":115},"content_hash":"033082259fddd34c9737b3676f110b496bffdb0b77119297cade5e63c6e1fff6"},"suggested_fix":"Move packageJson, licenseNotice, thirdPartyNotices (taking `web` as a parameter) and the declaration-rewrite step into a side-effect-free module such as web/scripts/sdk-package.mjs, keep build-sdk.mjs as the runner, and add web/scripts/sdk-package.test.ts with module-ID fixtures: a web/shell file (must throw), `@scope/pkg` and nested node_modules paths, a `?inline` query, a `\\0` helper ID, and a package without a license file.","summary":"The license guard and notice collection have no test, and build-sdk.mjs builds on import so they cannot be unit-tested","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:13:13.745043Z","id":"328ea8edd10fe9fefee7b5c0c93994a0c691ff0278468d17188cf8664712c506","body":{"detail":"The regex `^(?:import|export)\\b[^\"']*?from\\s*[\"'](\\.[^\"']+)[\"']` needs a `from`. Rollup writes a side-effect-only chunk dependency as `import \"./chunks/x.js\";` (and hoists transitive imports that way by default, output.hoistTransitiveImports), and a code-split lazy import as `import(\"./chunks/x.js\")`; a chunk reached only through either is left out of `sdkOverlay`, so the ceiling in web/perf/bundle-budget.json would stop covering code the entry loads. Today's build has none (overlay.js imports only `./index.js`, which imports `./chunks/client.js`), and the bundle-size.test.ts fixture (lines 90-93) covers only `from` imports, so nothing would notice when one appears.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":186},"end":{"line":192},"content_hash":"74ca573dd192e0013e7cbaa5c06ca793866ef9fa5abeb4357a6c2a0a24d0ee87"},"suggested_fix":"Match `^import\\s*[\"'](\\.[^\"']+)[\"']` and `\\bimport\\(\\s*[\"'](\\.[^\"']+)[\"']` too (or read the import graph from a Rollup manifest the SDK build writes), and add a fixture chunk reached only by a bare import to the bundle-size test.","summary":"The sdkOverlay walk follows only `import/export ... from` lines, so a bare `import \"./x.js\"` or a dynamic import() of another file is not counted","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:13:13.745081Z","id":"3072989f73a8dff22b945111f0908f189fc87af821d759d7ac7122b456e17372","body":{"detail":"The declarations are reachable only through the `types` condition in `exports`, which TypeScript reads under node16, nodenext and bundler but ignores under node10 (the default when `module` is commonjs). Such a project resolves `@empathic/clax-sdk` to index.js with no adjacent index.d.ts and `@empathic/clax-sdk/overlay` to nothing, so `strict` code fails with TS7016 (no declaration file). web/sdk/package.test.ts:121-146 type-checks only nodenext and bundler. The header comment (build-sdk.mjs:17-18) names those two resolutions, but neither docs/usage.md:621-654 nor the package says the others are unsupported.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"bf80416c55af3e76809f1c8a73050ff3c1d8af5dabc097a1dbe5e95e80fdd74d"},"suggested_fix":"Add `\"types\": \"./types/sdk/src/index.d.ts\"` and `\"typesVersions\": {\"*\": {\"overlay\": [\"./types/overlay/src/main.d.ts\"], \"service\": [\"./types/sdk/src/service.d.ts\"]}}` to packageJson(), and a node10 case to the package test; or state in docs/usage.md that the package's types need moduleResolution bundler, node16 or nodenext.","summary":"The package gives TypeScript projects on `moduleResolution: node` (node10) no types: there is no top-level `types` or `typesVersions`","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:13:13.745102Z","id":"499ded7e29c39f752abb3dbdce8932c97a03fca36229d5200f177bc690d57238","body":{"detail":"The build sets no build.target, so Vite's default ('modules': es2020, chrome87, safari14, firefox78, edge88) applies, and esbuild rewrites Svelte 5's `#private` fields and methods and public class fields: a build of this branch's web/dist-sdk/overlay.js starts with __privateAdd/__privateGet/__privateSet helpers and declares a WeakMap per field at top level (_started, _prev, _batches ... around its lines 907-922 and 2981-2997). The header says nothing is minified because the consumer's bundler minifies; downlevelling is likewise the consumer's job, and lowering here costs size (counted in sdkOverlay) and a WeakMap lookup per field access in Svelte's scheduler for every consumer, including those targeting current browsers. web/vite.bridge-parts.config.ts:13 already builds with target es2022.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":185},"end":{"line":188},"content_hash":"6566b9623d8106720c6ea2bc2771eb74e50c20488333276b1d568e9c242559b0"},"suggested_fix":"Set `target: \"es2022\"` (or \"esnext\") in build-sdk.mjs's build options, then re-measure sdkOverlay.","summary":"The package's code is lowered to Vite's default `modules` target, turning Svelte's private class fields into WeakMap helpers that a consumer's bundler cannot undo","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:17:08.245760Z","id":"f7da502c0eb904c3aa38ad8640cd478b2ab56d944411e4ce823d0e54e94bfc1b","body":{"detail":"A Vite 6.4.3 lib build in watch mode (build.watch: {}) of src/index.ts = `export { f } from \"./reporter\"; export type * from \"./types\";` with src/reporter.ts = `import type { T } from \"./types\"; ...` printed this.getWatchFiles() from writeBundle as [\"/src/index.ts\",\"/src/reporter.ts\"]: src/types.ts is not watched. On this branch web/sdk/src/types.ts declares only types and every import of it is type-only (sdk/src/index.ts:8 `export type * from \"./types\"`; reporter.ts:4, client.ts:3, service.ts:5, overlay/src/model.ts:6, Overlay.svelte:12, Reports.svelte:5 use `import type`), and web/overlay/src/options.ts is reached only by `import type` at overlay/src/main.ts:15. emitTypes() runs only from writeBundle (build-sdk.mjs:170-174), so an edit to either file leaves web/dist-sdk/types stale. scripts/watch.sh:81 starts the watch build; docs/usage.md:636-637 says it 'rebuilds it on every change to its sources'. The secondary point holds too: cleanOut(out) runs once at build-sdk.mjs:178 and emptyOutDir is false at line 186, and writeBundle writes but never removes files under chunks/ or types/. Cited lines are correct. Concern is the right kind: a dev-loop staleness, not a merge-blocking defect.","kind":"comment","references":"57f23d371629b772a3d1a5157a0a917716380660d4ffe77a76700019748b7109","summary":"confirmed: Vite's build watcher does not watch a module reached only by `import type`/`export type *`, so types/ goes stale in --watch","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:17:08.246117Z","id":"1d0e0c70cd08fbf11dba455b77840c693e548425a5a76e9a37840bfbe35fd225","body":{"detail":"build-sdk.mjs:123-127 builds the program with rootDir: web and emits declarations for every source file in it; visit() (lines 134-148) only rejects non-relative specifiers, missing declarations and reference directives, never the directory a declaration comes from. thirdPartyNotices() (lines 95-115) sees only bundled JavaScript module IDs (writeBundle, line 171), and a type-only import is erased before bundling, so it cannot catch such a reach. LICENSE:60-63 puts web/ (except extension, bridge, overlay, sdk) under AGPL-3.0-only, LICENSE:23/31 puts web/extension under GPL-2.0-only, LICENSE:65-71 puts web/sdk, web/overlay, web/bridge under LGPL-2.1-only; build-sdk.mjs:19-21 states the guarantee. web/sdk/package.test.ts:106-119 checks only that each declaration's specifiers stay inside the package and exist. web/overlay/src/options.ts:1-2 says it exists so main.ts's public types reach nothing of the bridge. Nothing reaches outside the three directories today; concern (an unguarded license boundary) is the right kind. Line citations hold.","kind":"comment","references":"a057dd22b8f18ad4f810f1b2fa5a12b7b67b54830e9ff61ea41fc5aa9bc314ea","summary":"confirmed: emitTypes() has no source-directory check, so a type-only reach into web/shell or web/extension would ship its declarations unchecked","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:17:08.246434Z","id":"cf197cbd49a7095395649446263a06a9aef2b55ea85883b8f0bc25406e1d697c","body":{"detail":"A Vite 6.4.3 lib build of src/main.js importing a CommonJS package node_modules/cjsdep (exports.hello = ...) gave chunk.modules keys [\"\\u0000<proj>/node_modules/cjsdep/index.js?commonjs-exports\", \"<proj>/node_modules/cjsdep/index.js\", \"\\u0000<proj>/node_modules/cjsdep/index.js?commonjs-es-import\", \"<proj>/src/main.js\"]. Running build-sdk.mjs:96-109 unchanged on the first two IDs produced two roots, one starting with \\u0000, and readFileSync(join(root, \"package.json\")) on it threw ERR_INVALID_ARG_VALUE \"The argument 'path' must be a string, Uint8Array, or URL without null bytes\". Vite 6.4.3's bundled commonjs plugin defines `const wrapId = (id, suffix) => `\\0${id}${suffix}`` and the four suffixes (vite/dist/node/chunks/dep-Dm0c1Wj2.js:2567-2583). Today's web/dist-sdk/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt lists only esm-env, modern-screenshot and svelte, so the current build is unaffected. The Windows point follows from lines 96 and 102 using path.sep against Vite's forward-slash IDs; not run, but no Windows build is exercised here. Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"9492ec6db6f9a986f5460ec2aea4ef0cc9bb76b395288001a183e2dfad7cc403","summary":"confirmed: a CommonJS dependency's `\\0`-prefixed IDs reach readFileSync with a null byte and fail the build","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:17:08.246792Z","id":"d113b791fbc67a94a29e8d29e18cf6f1ab97f1d475fe2dea92a1040be890f149","body":{"detail":"`grep -rn \"build-sdk\\|thirdPartyNotices\\|THIRD-PARTY\"` over the worktree's .ts/.mjs/.js/.bazel/.py/.sh files (excluding node_modules and dist-sdk) finds no test besides web/sdk/package.test.ts:71-76, which checks one real build's notices name svelte and modern-screenshot. build-sdk.mjs:178-191 runs cleanOut(out) and await build(...) at module top level, while PACKAGE_NAME (line 36) and ENTRIES (line 43) are exported but imported by nothing (grep finds them only in build-sdk.mjs). web/scripts/bundle-size.test.ts:30 and :95 copy bundle-size.mjs into a fixture tree and run it there. The untested path has a real defect (thread 9492ec6db6f9a986f5460ec2aea4ef0cc9bb76b395288001a183e2dfad7cc403: a `\\0` CommonJS ID crashes it), which supports concern as the kind. Line citations hold.","kind":"comment","references":"8a8d295a030821782b88de92ce8159a660cf7119aae639dce28cadbfafb0f331","summary":"confirmed: thirdPartyNotices() has no test of its failure path or ID shapes, and build-sdk.mjs builds at top level","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:17:08.247232Z","id":"70ebca64f4b34c3a03fdf0f08aedea151c39426515c4da6216c8f4d0d81f840c","body":{"detail":"web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs:190 matches /^(?:import|export)\\b[^\"']*?from\\s*[\"'](\\.[^\"']+)[\"']/gm; `import \"./chunks/x.js\";` has no `from` before its quote and `import(\"./x.js\")` is not at line start, so neither matches. Today's web/dist-sdk has none: `grep -nE \"^(import|export)|import\\(\"` finds only overlay.js:13 `import { ReporterClient } from \"./index.js\"`, index.js:4 and service.js:4 importing ./chunks/client.js. The test fixture's SDK files (web/scripts/bundle-size.test.ts:90-94; overlay graph at 91-93) use only `from` imports. Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"328ea8edd10fe9fefee7b5c0c93994a0c691ff0278468d17188cf8664712c506","summary":"confirmed: the sdkOverlay walk's regex needs `from`, so bare and dynamic imports are not followed","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:17:08.247628Z","id":"f92c0bfc49fe6c5574ec2fb2acb33d6cfeed3e7c396ebd5b328d2dde80ce8f9b","body":{"detail":"With TypeScript 5.9.3, a copy of web/dist-sdk as node_modules/@empathic/clax-sdk and app.ts importing ReporterClient from \"@empathic/clax-sdk\" and overlay from \"@empathic/clax-sdk/overlay\", createProgram({module: CommonJS, strict: true}) resolved moduleResolution to 2 (Node10) and reported `TS7016: Could not find a declaration file for module '@empathic/clax-sdk'. '.../index.js' implicitly has an 'any' type. There are types at '.../types/sdk/src/index.d.ts', but this result could not be resolved under your current 'moduleResolution' setting.` and the same for '@empathic/clax-sdk/overlay'; with moduleResolution Bundler there were no diagnostics. packageJson() (build-sdk.mjs:55-71) sets no top-level types or typesVersions; web/sdk/package.test.ts:121-146 checks only nodenext and bundler; docs/usage.md:621-654 does not mention moduleResolution. Off detail: `@empathic/clax-sdk/overlay` does not resolve 'to nothing' under node10; it resolves to overlay.js at the package root and fails with the same TS7016, not 'cannot find module'. Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"3072989f73a8dff22b945111f0908f189fc87af821d759d7ac7122b456e17372","summary":"confirmed: under node10 resolution both entries fail with TS7016; one supporting detail is off","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:17:08.248203Z","id":"8b88ba60963e84a920b4686bb23aa8085ce5ed2021f16287803e4c6b4b57f1f5","body":{"detail":"build-sdk.mjs:185-190 sets no target. Vite 6.4.3 defaults build.target to \"modules\" (vite/dist/node/chunks/dep-Dm0c1Wj2.js:46030, resolved at :46089) = ESBUILD_MODULES_TARGET [\"es2020\",\"edge88\",\"firefox78\",\"chrome87\",\"safari14\"] (vite/dist/node/constants.js:57-63). The branch's web/dist-sdk/overlay.js defines __privateGet/__privateAdd/__privateSet at lines 8-10 and __defNormalProp at line 5, and `grep -n \"new WeakMap\"` hits lines 907-921, 2981-2996, 3355 and 3529-3535 (_started, _prev, ... _decrement_queued; _anchor ... _effect_pending_subscriber), matching the cited ranges. web/vite.bridge-parts.config.ts:13 builds with target \"es2022\". Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"499ded7e29c39f752abb3dbdce8932c97a03fca36229d5200f177bc690d57238","summary":"confirmed: no build.target, so Vite's 'modules' target lowers Svelte's private and public class fields into helpers","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
